<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Why is the Sky Blue? / 为什么天空是蓝色的</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- English Column -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">English</span>
                <h2>For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
                <p>The sun sends us white light, but it is actually made of all the rainbow colors! When that light hits the air above, the blue color gets a bit silly and scatters all over the place like a bouncy ball. So, when you look up, you see all that beautiful blue floating around!</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">English</span>
                <h2>For a High School Teenager</h2>
                <p>The sky is blue because of a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight reaches Earth's atmosphere and is scattered by the gas molecules and particles in the air. Blue light travels in shorter, smaller waves than other colors like red or yellow. Because blue waves are shorter, they get scattered much more than the other colors, which is why when you look up, your eyes catch all that scattered blue light coming from every part of the sky.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">English</span>
                <h2>For a Physics PhD</h2>
                <p>The blue color of the sky is primarily the result of Rayleigh scattering of electromagnetic radiation by atmospheric particles much smaller than the wavelength of the incident light. The intensity of the scattered light is inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength ($I \propto \lambda^{-4}$). Since solar radiation peaks in the visible spectrum and the shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) are scattered significantly more efficiently than the longer wavelengths (red), the observed spectral distribution of the sky light is dominated by blue. Furthermore, the human eye is less sensitive to violet compared to blue, resulting in the perception of a pale blue sky.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Chinese Column -->
        <div class="column">
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
                <h2>给 3 岁宝宝</h2>
                <p>太阳向我们发送白光，但它实际上包含了彩虹里所有的颜色！当这些光撞击上方的空气时，蓝色变得很调皮，像弹球一样到处乱蹦跳去。所以，当你抬头看时，你会看到到处都是漂浮的蓝色！</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
                <h2>给高中生</h2>
                <p>天空之所以是蓝色的是因为一种被称为瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）的现象。阳光到达地球大气层，被空气中的气体分子和颗粒散射。蓝光的波长比红光或黄光等颜色更短、更小。因为蓝光波长较短，它们比其他颜色散射得厉害得多，这就是为什么当我们抬头看时，我们的眼睛会捕捉到来自天空各个部分的散射蓝光。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="section">
                <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
                <h2>给物理学博士</h2>
                <p>天空呈现蓝色主要是由于电磁辐射在粒径远小于入射光波长的大气颗粒上发生瑞利散射的结果。散射光线的强度与波长的四次方成反比（$I \propto \lambda^{-4}$）。由于太阳辐射在可见光谱中达到峰值，且短波长（蓝光和紫光）比长波长的散射效率高得多，因此观测到的天空光光谱分布以蓝光为主导。此外，人眼对紫光的敏感度低于蓝光，导致感知到的天空为浅蓝色。</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
